WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.940
Do the same cells set the clock and narrow the pupil?

2
00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.480
Or do separate cells do each job?

3
00:00:09.483 --> 00:00:12.323
To find out, you need a way to mark one set of cells.

4
00:00:13.223 --> 00:00:14.983
Here the marker is Brn3b.

5
00:00:16.823 --> 00:00:18.923
Brn3b is a transcription factor.

6
00:00:19.823 --> 00:00:23.683
Most ganglion cells make it, but a subset of M1 cells does not.

7
00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:29.003
In 2011, Chen, Badea and Hattar traced where each set goes.

8
00:00:30.727 --> 00:00:34.387
Brn3b-negative M1 cells reached the SCN, the clock.

9
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:42.600
Brn3b-positive cells reached the olivary pretectal nucleus, which drives the pupil.

10
00:00:43.683 --> 00:00:51.563
Predict. Kill only the Brn3b-positive ipRGCs, leaving other ganglion cells intact.

11
00:00:52.483 --> 00:00:53.563
What happens to the pupil?

12
00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:55.583
And to the clock?

13
00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:03.667
The pupil light reflex was severely impaired.

14
00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.467
But circadian photoentrainment was spared.

15
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.960
The Brn3b-negative cells that reach the SCN were still there.

16
00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.900
So the two behaviours depend on partly different cells.

17
00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.220
The outputs can be pulled apart.

18
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.420
Notice what the marker defines here.

19
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.140
Brn three B marks an output set, not one morphological type.

20
00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.650
Those outputs come from a varied population.

21
00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.690
Mouse ipRGCs are named M1 to M6.

22
00:01:34.733 --> 00:01:39.173
They differ in shape, in where their dendrites sit, and in where their axons go.

23
00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:43.327
M1 cells are the classic clock and pupil cells.

24
00:01:44.227 --> 00:01:46.967
Their dendrites lie in the outermost stratum of that layer.

25
00:01:47.967 --> 00:01:50.447
That stratum is conventionally called OFF.

26
00:01:51.227 --> 00:01:54.767
The name describes where the dendrites sit, not the cell's own response.

27
00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.190
M2 dendrites lie in the inner band.

28
00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:01.330
M3 cells have dendrites in both bands.

29
00:02:02.383 --> 00:02:07.423
M4 is the mouse sustained ON alpha cell, and it is intrinsically photosensitive.

30
00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:13.847
M5 and M6 send axons to the thalamic relay for image-forming vision.

31
00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:16.447
The letters name mouse cells.

32
00:02:17.307 --> 00:02:19.127
They are not six matching human types.

33
00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:23.187
A marker can separate the clock route from the pupil route.

34
00:02:24.027 --> 00:02:27.067
It cannot, by itself, name the subtype behind each job.
